+# Major mathematical repair: canonical infinite route and finite active roots
+
+## Decision
+
+The duplicate ambient Experimental branch is no longer executable mathematics. Its four roots required a nonexistent scalar-generic double-angle functional calculus, a missing spectral-theorem import, and concrete infinite-dimensional ideal classes that were never constructed. Ninety-one descendant modules inherited those assumptions. `GraphSubspace.lean` separately relied on a missing acute-to-bounded-graph theorem whose generic signature was never supported.
+
+The repository already contains the paper-facing unbounded sine, double-angle, tangent-two-theta, complexification, PVM, resolvent, and abstract ideal theory in production and vendored Spectra modules. The affected historical paths are therefore compatibility imports to the canonical aggregate, not alternate theorem implementations.
+
+No historical source was discarded. The complete pre-repair text is in `dev/retired-infinite-dimensional-facades-2026-07-21.tar.gz`.
+
+## Finite mathematics that remains active
+
+- `DirectRotation/PrincipalPlanes.lean`: canonical singular-vector principal planes and restricted-displacement geometry.
+- `DirectRotation/Majorization.lean`: Davis restricted-displacement Ky Fan and UI-norm minimality.
+- `Experimental/FiniteDimensional/Generalized.lean`: whitening and arbitrary-separation residual estimates.
+- `Experimental/FiniteDimensional/Sharpness.lean`: explicit planar equality models.
+
+These files are not hidden from status reporting. The root checker compiles each registered file and then the full Experimental target.
+
